2026-09-19 04:19 Fixed. lib/IO/K8s/AutoGen.pm: added _overrequires() and a required-compatibility
filter in _core_class_for (k136) -- a reuse candidate is dropped if it marks a
shared key `required` (plain or `required=>'schema'`) that the schema's own
`required` list leaves optional. Only applied when the schema declares a
`required` key at all (absent `required` is treated as "no claim", not
"nothing required" -- real upstream schemas for LabelSelector/{key,operator,
values}/{name,value} always declare required explicitly when relevant, so
this changes nothing for them; it protects those ~140/~160 established
reuses from a fixture/third-party schema that simply omits `required`).
Verified via t/75_reuse_core.t and t/98_k120_overlay_semantics.t, which
initially broke with the naive "absent==empty" semantics and now pass.

Result for CertManager/PrometheusOperator: the fix removes the *data-loss*
risk (reuse_core no longer picks Meta::V1::Condition, whose required
message/reason/lastTransitionTime don't match the CRD's [status,type] or
[lastTransitionTime,status,type]) but does NOT make the emitter render the
provider-owned classes -- reuse_core is purely structural/type/required
compatibility, not domain-aware, so for the 6-key (with observedGeneration)
